## Locked sizes @ 1468×2048 (layout.00001)

| Element | Rule | ≈ px |
|---------|------|------|
| Avatar diameter | `max(151, int(w*0.195) - 1)` | **285** |
| Avatar gap X | `max(30, w//48)` | ~30 |
| Avatar gap Y | `max(16, w//72)` | ~20 |
| Name size | `max(46, int(w*0.064))` | **93** |
| Name stroke | `max(1, name_size//28)` | **3** |
| Name tracking | `max(1, name_size//47)` | **1** |
| Name clear above pillar | `max(10, pillar_gap + stroke + 23 - 3)` | ~34 |
| Name flush (right) | `stroke_w - 9` | pulls slightly inside cap |
| Bio size | `max(16, min(pill_h*0.42, w*0.028))`, shrink-to-fit ≥11 | **~37** before shrink |

## Rebake snapshots

`tools/rizcard_preview.py` does **not** write `output/_hud_*.png`. To update disk previews, call `render_rizcard` and `write_bytes` to `output/_hud_0000N.png`.

## Next rizcards

Reuse these `_HUD_*` ratios/sizes unless the user asks to retune. Special layouts keep their own path (e.g. layout 37).
